<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37887" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-rōdo</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, sum, 3, v.
				a.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To gnaw in front</i>, <i>to gnaw at
				the end</i> or <i>tip</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">digitos suos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 3, 2, 93</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">teneros pampinos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. Arbor. 15</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To gnaw</i>, <i>bite</i>, or <i>nibble off</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praeroso hamo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 5, 25</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praerosa dentibus lingua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 23, 23, § 87</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conger et muraena caudas inter se praerodentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 9,
					62, 88, § 185</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
